  "manual_conclusions": [
    "FixtureContextStore creates one local service/policy from constructor-supplied finite grants; write wrapper issues an invocation only under that service and owns product admission_transaction. It does not union a mutation into grants, retry denied mutations or adopt arbitrary caller SQL transactions.",
    "FixturePolicy._lease_locked enforces fixture-user/provider_intake, dependency subset of finite grants, explicit deny intersection, and revision checks; grant setters remain explicit test controls.",
    "fixture_context all_selected=True selects from a request; policy grants remain finite independently. No fixture issuer imports into src were found.",
    "Module-wide grant declarations include synthetic absent/foreign coordinates only to exercise later validators; permission controls independently enforce out-of-grant refusals and expiry. Successful deeper query tests do not establish Provider/Exchange or Recovery composition.",
    "Nine Access roundtrip variants explicitly select include_context=False on already Core-only catalogs; their Core assertion ASTs remain unchanged and Context routes stay refused."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Finite declarations are module-scoped synthetic fixture grants, sometimes broader than one individual test mutation, but contain explicit named identities and no runtime-generated permission expansion on refusal.",
    "Fresh full suite outcomes and actual policy counterexamples are tracked by parent report and authorization agent separately."
  ]
